{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1385303-the-magnus-archives-spoilers","id":1385303,"title":"The Magnus Archives (spoilers)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T14:43:28-07:00","id":1385303,"title":"The Magnus Archives (spoilers)","content":"Hi guys.<br /> <br /> I'll just start by saying, I'm not the biggest fan of Beast. I think there's potential there, but for me, it needs more work to really shine. As have some of the other CofD lines, looking at the incredible 2es we've gotten (looking at you Geist).<br /> <br /> However, considering the controversy, I'm not sure how likely we are to get a second run at this line (interested in seeing what others think on that).<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I was catching up on Magnus Archives today and some of the most recent episodes, it clicked with me.<br /> <br /> SPOILERS FOR S4 MAGNUS ARCHIVES<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, we have groups of people who are avatars of terror/fear/powers, who started off human, but slowly lost their humanity while gaining special abilities. But now, they need to feed (Statement Begins). Sound familiar?<br /> <br /> For me, this really hits well as a good understanding of how beast works, and what kind of balance they play. Remaining human while balancing the hunger. Be interested in other people's thoughts, or if I'm way out there on my own.<br /> <br /> Personally I'm not a fan of the entirely dreamland aspects of beast, or the fact all monsters like them etc. Not sure how you'd redo heroes either.<br /> <br /> I realise as I'm typing I'm mostly thinking out loud now. Anyhow, interested in people's thoughts, and I'll delete this if it's of no merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T18:16:39-07:00","id":1385332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1385303-the-magnus-archives-spoilers#post1385303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I'm not a fan of the entirely dreamland aspects of beast,</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The entirely dreamland aspects of Beast&quot; are the fact that their monstrous elements come from a psychic landscape of pure idea. Despite being the Astral shamanoid splat, many Beasts have no direct engagement with the rest of the Astral outside of their Lairs and hives, barring interactions with kin pulling them further afield.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or the fact all monsters like them etc. </div> </div> </div>Being able to be especially persuasive to monsters as long as you haven't done anything to lose their trust is not &quot;all monsters like them.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not sure how you'd redo heroes either. </div> </div> </div>The fact that Heroes are almost completely orthogonal to the Begotten's own experience is kind of the point \u2014 they're human folklore imposing itself on them through the Temenos in a way that variously ignores or denies their actual history as people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T00:50:40-07:00","id":1385371,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input, you make some really good clarifications. I don't think I'm explaining myself well enough tbh.<br /> <br /> How do I delete my first post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T01:35:10-07:00","id":1385378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1385303-the-magnus-archives-spoilers?p=1385371#post1385371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the input, you make some really good clarifications. I don't think I'm explaining myself well enough tbh.<br /> <br /> How do I delete my first post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t delete your post that isn\u2019t necessary. Your allowed to have opinions. Eventually they may return and do more Beast, but probably not soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:01:54-07:00","id":1385479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baileyborough</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1385303-the-magnus-archives-spoilers?p=1385371#post1385371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the input, you make some really good clarifications. I don't think I'm explaining myself well enough tbh.<br /> <br /> How do I delete my first post?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just clarify what you mean, you don't need to delete the start of it. If it came off extremely different from what you'd intended you can just edit the starting post. Though there's no issue with just clarifying what you meant and such.<br /> <br /> From what I'm gathering it seems like you're more interested in the Life v Legend play that doesn't see as much disccussion for Beast then just the feeding aspects?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}